          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கோபம் (kōpam) — \"anger\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Anger — the ordinary everyday word for it, not a literary one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You can read all of it already, and one part of it you only just learned: கோ is க with the ◌ோ sign, the sign whose free-standing letter ஓ you met last chapter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It ends in ம், like வணக்கம், தூக்கம் and பணம் before it. That ending is now four words deep, and it is a good bet for a Tamil noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five feelings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
