    {
      "id": "TA-W27-read-payam",
      "sequence": 2930,
      "title": "பயம் (payam) — a word with no vowel signs",
      "headword": "பயம்",
      "romanization": "payam",
      "gloss": "the word for fear on the page — three letters and no signs at all",
      "script": "tamil",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-type",
        "script-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:f7282420d75d4462",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [
          "a pen and something to write on",
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Script you'll notice: பயம் — a word with no vowel signs",
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You will want a pen and something to write on and your eyes, for letter shapes on the page. You can listen to everything else now — leave the sections called Script you'll notice: பயம் — a word with no vowel signs and Guided Practice until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the page: you can say kōpam and payam. Now read the second one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: பயம் — a word with no vowel signs",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Every word you have read so far carried at least one sign. பயம் (payam) carries none, and that makes it the clearest possible demonstration of what a bare Tamil letter is worth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "piece",
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 3,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "piece: ப, pa, no sign — the letter's own built-in a is the vowel.",
                "piece: ய, ya, the same again.",
                "piece: ம், m, ம with a புள்ளி, so no vowel at all."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ப, ய, ம் becomes பயம் (payam)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So a Tamil consonant is never really silent by default. It says a unless something stops it, and the only thing that stops it is the dot. Read the word once and hear the two a sounds you were never told about."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "READ",
              "instruction": "ப — then ய — then ம்",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU READ: **ப** — then **ய** — then **ம்**]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "POINT",
              "instruction": "the one mark in the whole word, and say what it does",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU POINT: the one mark in the whole word, and say what it does]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "READ",
              "instruction": "பயம் (payam), then கடை, and say which one needed a sign",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU READ: **பயம்**, then **கடை**, and say which one needed a sign]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say kōpam, then say payam, then read பயம்",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *kōpam*, then say *payam*, then read **பயம்**]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Read பயம் (payam). Which vowel do ப and ய carry, and why is none written? (a — it is built into the letter.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
